## 14. SOC Interview Questions

**Q1. What is Wireshark?**  
A network protocol analyser used to capture and inspect network packets.

**Q2. What is the difference between a capture filter and a display filter?**  
A capture filter limits which packets are collected; a display filter controls which already-captured packets are shown.

**Q3. What does DNS do?**  
DNS translates domain names into records such as IP addresses and other service information.

**Q4. What is a TCP SYN packet?**  
It is a TCP flag commonly used to initiate a connection.

**Q5. Can Wireshark show the contents of every HTTPS request?**  
No. HTTPS encrypts application data, so full request contents are generally not readable from a normal packet capture.

**Q6. Does a TCP retransmission prove malicious activity?**  
No. Retransmissions can result from packet loss, congestion, or network conditions.

